# Keep image builds lean: bulk data never enters the context, but DVC
# pointer files (*.dvc) do — the serving entrypoint pulls the real bytes
# from R2 at boot. Cloud checkouts are already clean (data/ is gitignored);
# this guards local `docker build` against the 64 GB FITS cache.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/tables/labels/
# Same trailing-slash trick as models/cv below: exclude the bulk, re-include
# the pointers. The entrypoint pulls one 1.3 MB file out of
# candidates_viewset/ to derive the observation baseline, and it cannot
# resolve a pointer that never reached the image.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/*.dvc
data/tables/catalogue/
data/csv/exofop/
# The API reads exactly three things under models/: cv, history and
# registry.json. Everything else is an experimental arm — phase1, phase1a and
# stage9 were 248 MB of the 1.6 GB context, and the Dockerfile COPYs models/
# wholesale, so they were in the image too. Deny by default and name what is
# served, so the next arm directory does not leak the way these three did.
models/*
!models/cv
!models/history
!models/registry.json
# Docker strips the trailing slash, so this also swallows the *.dvc pointer
# files the entrypoint pulls with — re-include them explicitly.
models/cv/*/
!models/cv/*.dvc
**/mlruns/
# Same trailing-slash trick as models/cv: exclude the bulk, re-include the
# pointer. results/candidates_scored.parquet is the catalogue's P(planet)
# column and the API reads it at request time.
results/*
!results/*.dvc
outputs/
multirun/
.phase1-scratch/
node_modules/
frontend/design-console/dist/
frontend/node_modules/
.dvc/cache/
.dvc/tmp/
# Live R2 credentials. The Dockerfile only COPYs .dvc/config, so this never
# reached an image layer — but the build context is uploaded wholesale to the
# remote builder, so keep it out of the tarball too.
.dvc/config.local
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
mlflow.db
